out prior notice to the Client if the Client violates one or more of the terms of this Agreement. <br> 10.3.This Agreement is considered terminated in relation to the Parties with the moment of full fulfillment by the Client and the Company of mutual obligations under the earlier performed non-trading operations and repayment of all debts of each of Of the Parties to the Agreement, provided that there are no unfulfilled obligations under this Agreement. <br> </p>',
    "landing_privacy" => "Privacy policy",
    "landing_privacy_text" => "1. When registering at ".config('app.domain').", the Client provides certain personal data, including information necessary to prevent the legalization of illegally obtained funds. <br> 1.1 The company collects and stores the following information on the client: Email address, encrypted password, full client's name and address. <br> 2. The client undertakes to provide correct, accurate and updated personal data, and must not impersonate another natural or legal person. In the event of a change in the data, the Client is obliged to notify the Company immediately or within 30 days after such a change. <br> 2.1 Information about the Client, which was or will be provided by the Client during his use of ".config('app.domain')." services, can be used by the Company to send advertising messages to the Client. <br> 2.2 The Client's details that were and / or will be provided by the Client in the course of his / her actions on the Site may be disclosed by the Company to state authorities. The Company will disclose such information only if required from the Company by applicable law, regulation or court order to the minimum required amount. <br> 2.3 Information about a client that does not have a private status may be used in advertising materials. <br> 3. Based on the preliminary conditions for conducting Transactions on the Site, the Company has the right to require the Client to provide certain certification or other documents. If the Client does not submit such documents to the Company, then the Company, at its discretion, may freeze the Client's Account for any period of time, or permanently close the Account. Without limiting the provisions of the Privacy Policy, the Company may, at its sole discretion, refuse to open an Account to any individual or legal entity with or without specifying a reason. <br> 4. In case of registration on ".config('app.domain').", a person on behalf of a corporation or other commercial organization, such registration is considered a registration of a representative of a corporation or organization under which that person is authorized to represent such a corporation or organization as a Client. <br> 5. The company has the right to disclose private information about its current or former Clients only if the Client gives written consent to such disclosure, or such disclosure is required by applicable law or to verify the identity of the Client. The Client's information is transferred only to those employees of the Company who are in charge of the Client Accounts. Any such information must be stored on electronic or other media in accordance with the requirements of applicable law. <br> 6. The Client confirms and agrees that all or part of the information on the Client's Account and Operations is stored in the Company and can be used by the Company in the event of a dispute between the Client and the Company. <br> 7. The Company, at its sole discretion, may, but is not obligated, to view and verify any information provided by the Client, for any purpose. The Client hereby accepts and agrees to that the Company is not liable to the Client in connection with the above viewing or verification of information. <br> 8. The Company is obliged to take measures to implement improved data protection procedures and to update them periodically in order to protect private information about Clients and their Accounts. <br> 9 When registering at ".config('app.domain').", the Client chooses the username and password used by the Client each time he logs into the Site, as well as for conducting Operations and using the Company's Services. To maintain the confidentiality of the Client's information on ".config('app.domain').", the Client is strictly prohibited from disclosing registration data to other persons or commercial organizations, including, but not limited to, a username and password. The company is not responsible for any damage or loss, caused to the Client due to improper use (including prohibited and unprotected use) or storage of his username and password, including any such use by third parties authorized or not authorized by the Client. <br> 10. The Client is solely responsible for using ".config('app.domain')." under his own name and a password. The Company is not responsible for any such use, including checking what exactly the Client does with his Account. <br> 11. The Client is obliged to immediately notify the Company's customer support service of any suspicion of unauthorized use of the Account. <br> 12. The Company does not collects and does not store customer credit card information. <br> In accordance with the recommendations of the Payment Card Industry Security Standards Council (PCI DSS), to protect customer data, encryption is used at the transport level - TLS 1.2 and at the application level with the AES algorithm with a key length of 256 bits. <br> 13. Definition of \"Cookies\" : <br> A cookie is a small set of data that often includes an anonymous unique identifier that is sent to the web browser of the Client's computer or mobile phone (hereinafter referred to as the “device”) from the computers of the website and stored on the hard disk the Client's computer. Each website can send its own cookie to the Client's web browser, if allowed by its settings, however, for privacy reasons, the Client's web browser allows the website to access only those cookies that it has already sent to the Client's computer, and not cookies that have been sent by other sites. Many websites use cookies every time a user visits them in order to track online traffic. By changing the settings and properties of the browser, the Client can set such a configuration of his web browser that will block the access of cookies to his computer. <br> Our policy regarding cookies: when visiting the ".config('app.domain')." website, the pages viewed and cookies are downloaded to the hard drive of the Client's device. Cookies stored on your hard drive can be used for anonymous identification in the event of a repeated visit of the Client to the website and to determine the most popular pages of the website among our Clients. However, for confidentiality and security purposes, the Company does not store personal data of Clients, including full name, personal information, email addresses, etc. The use of cookies is common. Most major websites today use this technology. Cookies stored on the hard drive of the Client's device allow ".config('app.domain')." to create the most convenient and effective website for the Company's Clients, allowing us to find out the preferences of our Clients. <br> 14. The mobile application can send anonymous data about installed programs . <br> ",
    "landing_kyc" => " AML and KYC Policy",
    "landing_kyc_sub" => 'Anti Money Laundering (AML) Policy and Know Your Customer (KYC) Policy',
    "landing_kyc_text" => " 1. The AML and KYC policy applies to ".config('app.domain')." and its partners and Clients (hereinafter the \"Company\") and has the goal of discouraging and actively preventing money laundering and any other activity that facilitates money laundering or the financing of terrorist or criminal activities. The Company requires its managers, employees and affiliates to follow the principles of this Policy in order to prevent the use of its services for money laundering. <br> 2. Within the framework of this Policy, as a rule, actions are, aimed at concealing or distorting the true origin of funds obtained by criminal means, with the aim of laundering illegal proceeds. <br> 3. Usually, money laundering occurs in three stages. Initially, during the “placement” stage, cash enters the financial system, where the money obtained from criminal activities is converted into monetary instruments such as money orders, travelers checks, or deposited in accounts with financial institutions. During the “layering” stage, funds are transferred or moved to other accounts or other financial institutions to further separate the money from its criminal origin. During the “integration” stage, funds are returned to the economy and used to purchase property, finance business or criminal activity. Terrorist financing may not use the proceeds of criminal activity; most likely this is an attempt to hide the origin or the alleged use of funds that will subsequently be used for criminal purposes. <br> 4. The client undertakes to: <br> comply with legal norms, including international ones, aimed at combating illegal trade, financial fraud, laundering and legalization of funds obtained by illegal means; <br> exclude direct or indirect complicity in illegal financial activities and any other illegal operations using the Site. <br> 5. The client guarantees legal origin, All personal and official documentation will be kept for the minimum period of time established by local legislation. <br> 9. All new employees are required to undergo training in AML and KYC. Existing employees are trained annually. Participation in additional training programs is mandatory for all employees related to AML and KYC. <br> 10. The Company has the right to require the Client to confirm his registration information specified when opening a trading account at his own discretion and at any time. In order to verify the data, the Company may request from the Client the provision of notarized copies of: passport, license or national identity card for identity confirmation; bank statements or utility bills to confirm residential address. In special cases, the Company may ask the Client to provide a photograph of the Client holding an identity card next to his face. Detailed requirements for identifying clients are specified in the \"AML Policy\" section on the official website of the Company. <br> 11. The procedure for verifying the Client's identification data is optional, provided that the client has not received such a request from the company. The client may voluntarily send a copy of his passport or other document confirming his identity to the Company's customer service department to ensure verification of the specified personal data. The client should take into account that when making deposits / withdrawals by bank transfer, it is necessary to provide documents for full verification of the name and address in connection with the specifics of the implementation and processing of banking transactions. <br> 12. If any of the Client's registration data (full name, address or phone number) have been changed, the Client is obliged to immediately make the appropriate changes to the data specified in the personal profile in the Company or notify the customer service department of the Company about such changes. <br> 12.1. To change the phone number indicated during the registration of the client profile, we require you to provide a document confirming the right to own the new number (agreement with a mobile provider), and a photo of the identity document that the client holds next to his face. The client's personal data in both documents must match. <br>",
    "landing_payment_privacy" => "Payment policy",
    "landing_payment_privacy_text" => "1.1 The amount of the Client's account balance is the amount of the Company's financial obligations to the client at a specific time. <br> 1.2 The Company's financial obligations to the Client arise from the moment the account appears on the deposit of funds to the account and end at the moment the Client withdraws funds in full from the account. < br> 1.3 The Client has the right to demand from the Company the fulfillment of obligations in an amount not exceeding the value of the account balance. <br> 1.4 The official methods of depositing / withdrawing funds are the Company's wallets / accounts in those payment systems indicated on the Company's website. The Client assumes all risks associated with the use of payment systems, since payment systems are not partners of the Company. The Company is not responsible for the delay and / or non-receipt of funds on the balance of the Client's account due to the fault of the payment system. In the event of any claims from the Client regarding the correct operation of payment systems, the Client should contact the support service of such a payment system. The Client is obliged to notify about cases of such requests. <br> 1.5 The Company is not responsible for the actions of third parties who carry out intermediary activities in the Clients' operations for depositing / withdrawing funds. When the Client conducts deposit operations, the financial responsibility of the Company begins from the moment the Client's funds are received into the bank account of the Company and / or to the account of the Company in the payment systems specified on the Company's website. In case of revealing signs of fraud in the implementation of financial transactions after funds are credited to the balance of the Client's account, the Company reserves the right to cancel this transaction and freeze the client's account. When Clients carry out operations to withdraw funds, the financial responsibility of the Company ends at the time of debiting funds from the Company's bank account and / or from the Company's account in the payment systems specified on the Company's website. <br> 1.6 In case of technical errors on the part of the Company when making financial transactions , The Company reserves the right to cancel such transactions and their results, as well as the results of the services provided by the Company. <br> 1.7 The Client is obliged to register only 1 (one) account with the Company. If multiple accounts are identified, belonging to one Client, all such accounts will be blocked, and the funds contained on them will not be subject to withdrawal. <br> 2. Registration of a client and his data <br> 2.1 The procedure for registering a client consists of 2 stages: <br> - the procedure for registering the Client on the Company's website; <br> - the procedure for verifying the identity and data specified during registration. <br> The procedure for registering the Client is mandatory for the Client of the Company. To complete the procedure for registering a Client on the Company's website, you must perform the following actions: <br> - enter personal and contact information; <br> - accept the terms of this Agreement and its annexes. <br> 2. 2 The procedure for verifying the identity and data is carried out by the Company to confirm the correctness and completeness of the data specified by the Client during registration. To carry out this procedure, the Company is obliged to require, and the Client is obliged to provide: <br> - a scan or digital photograph of a General Civil, Foreign Passport or other document proving the Client's identity in a readable form. For citizens of the Russian Federation - spread of the page (s) with a photograph and personal data. For citizens of Ukraine - page (s) with a photo and personal data in Russian and Ukrainian (if available). <br> - For citizens of other countries - page (s) of a passport with a photo and personal data or other document (for example, ID Card ) containing a photo and personal data. <br> Additionally, the Company has the right to demand current utility bills, an agreement with a bank on opening a personal account, scans of bank cards, as well as any other documents if the above documents do not fully identify the Client and / or the personal data specified by him. <br> 2.3 The procedure for verifying the identity and data must be carried out within 10 (ten) business days from the date the Company submits a request to verify the identity of the Client. In some cases, it is allowed to increase this period up to 30 (thirty) working days at the discretion of the Company. <br> 3. Deposit procedures <br> In order to deposit funds into the account, the Client must submit an application for depositing funds from his personal account. To do this, the Client must choose one of the payment systems, indicated on the Company's website and follow the appropriate link indicating all the necessary data. <br> The following currencies are available for replenishing the account: USD <br> The processing time for a deposit request depends on the selected payment system and cannot be settled by the Company. If there is a technical feasibility, input transactions using electronic payment systems can take place instantly. When using a bank transfer, the terms can be from 3 to 45 working days, depending on the bank used by the Client and correspondent banks. <br> Any transactions made by the Client must be carried out through a specific transaction source owned exclusively by the Client, who pays with his by own means. Withdrawal, return, compensation and other payments made from the Client's account can only be made using the same account (bank or payment card) that was used to deposit funds. Withdrawals from the Account can only be made in the currency in which the respective deposit was made. <br> 4. Taxes <br> The company is not a tax agent and does not provide data on the operations of its clients to third parties. Such information can be provided only if there is an official request from the competent state authorities. <br> 5. Refund Policy <br> 5.1 The Client has the right at any time to withdraw part or all of the funds from his Account by sending the Company a request for withdrawal of funds, which contains the Client's order to withdraw money from the Client's Account and meets the following conditions: <br> - The Company performs withdrawals from the Client's trading account only within the limits of the Client's account balance during the execution of the order. If the amount of the Client's withdrawal (including commissions and other payment costs in accordance with these Regulations) exceeds the balance on the Client's Account, the Company may reject the withdrawal after clarification .; <br> - the Client's order to withdraw funds from the Client's Account must comply with the requirements and restrictions, established by current legislation and other provisions in force in the countries in whose jurisdiction such a transfer is made; <br> - funds from the Client's Account must be withdrawn to the same payment system and the same wallet ID, which was previously used by the Client to transfer funds to the Account. The Company can limit the withdrawal to the client's payment system within the amount of the deposit received to the Client's account from this payment system. The Company may, at its discretion, make exceptions to this rule and withdraw the Client's funds to other payment systems, while the Company may at any time request payment information from the Client on other payment systems, and the Client must provide the Company with such payment information .; <br> 5.2 A request for withdrawal of funds is carried out by transferring money to the external account of the Client by an Agent authorized by the Company. <br> 5.3 The Client generates a request for withdrawal of funds in the currency of the deposit. If the deposit currency differs from the transfer currency, The Company converts the withdrawal amount into the currency of the transfer at the exchange rate established by the Company at the time of withdrawal of funds from the Client's Account. <br> 5.4 The currency in which the Company makes transfers to the Client's External Account, depending on the currency of the Client's Account and the withdrawal method, may be displayed in Client's personal account. <br> 5.5 Conversion, commissions and other costs associated with each withdrawal method are set by the Company and can be changed at any time at the Company's sole discretion. The exchange rate may differ from the exchange rate set by the authorities of the particular country and the current market exchange rate for the respective currencies. In the cases established by the Payment Service Providers, funds can be withdrawn from the Client's account in the currency, other than the currency of the Client's External Account. <br> 5.6 The Company reserves the right to set minimum and maximum withdrawal amounts depending on the withdrawal method. These restrictions will be posted in the Client's Personal Account. <br> 5.7 A withdrawal request is considered accepted by the Company if it is created in the Client's Personal Account and is indicated in the \"History of Balance Transactions\" section as well as in the Company's system to record client requests. A withdrawal request created in any way other than the one specified in this clause will not be accepted and executed by the Company. <br> 5.8 The money will be withdrawn from the Client's account within 5 (five) business days. <br> 5.9 If the funds sent by the Company to according to the withdrawal request, 1 The client can send a request for withdrawal of funds by bank transfer at any time if the Company provides this method at the time of the transfer of funds. <br> 6.1.2 The client can apply for withdrawal of funds only to a bank account opened in his name. The Company does not accept and does not carry out transfers of funds to bank accounts of third parties. <br> 6.1.3 The Company must send funds to the Client's bank account in accordance with the information specified in the request for withdrawal of funds, if the conditions of section 7.1.2. of these Rules are observed. <br> The client understands and agrees that the Company is not responsible for the time it takes to complete a bank transfer. <br> 6.2 Wire transfer. <br> 6.2. 3 The Company may, at its discretion, offer the Client other ways to withdraw funds from the Client's account. This information is published in the Personal Account. <br>",
